  "notes": [
    "With skill 37/38 (97%) vs baseline 21/38 (55%), essentially the same gap as iteration 1 (38/38 vs 21/38 on the 19-check grader). The iteration-1 skill fixes held: no hydration errors, eslint clean with no hand edits, no font fallback, no stale Bklit errors reaching the console.",
    "The one with-skill miss is real and is the skill's own fault: its advice to 'start ./node_modules/.bin/next start and kill that PID' orphans next-server, because `next start` is a wrapper that spawns it. The guidance is now `pkill -P $PID; kill $PID`, and screenshot.mjs kills the whole process tree.",
    "Caveat: iteration-1 'no server left' passes are vacuous. I had already cleaned up those servers before the check existed.",
    "Grader bug found by a with-skill agent: with isMobile, Chromium widens innerWidth to fit overflowing content, so a scrollWidth-vs-innerWidth check can never fail. Fixed in both probe.mjs and screenshot.mjs (compare against the device width). After the fix, both iterations still show no real mobile overflow.",
    "Time-to-message (new check): the cinematic baseline hid its h1 at 1.5s in BOTH iterations (long title-sequence intro). The skill's runs never did. This is the clearest quality discriminator that doesn't depend on the stack.",
    "Convergence risk (qualitative): with-skill runs land on near-identical art direction across iterations. Nocturne used Instrument Serif + amber + 'Every frame, graded\u2026' both times; Relay used Anton + oklch(0.7 0.215 38) both times. The skill's first-row examples likely anchor these choices.",
    "Cost: the skill uses ~1.4x the time and ~1.8x the tokens of the baseline, mostly scaffold/registry installs, the flowy pass, and screenshot-fix loops."
  ]
